    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0714" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1945v01/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/5–845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chairman of the United States Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-08">May 8, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. At his press conference yesterday<anchor n="47" xml:id="d218-f1"/>
                    Molotov is reported to have stated that
                    Russia will take the initiative in having the International Organization clothed
                    with power actively to promote self-government for dependent peoples. Although
                    this has been our historic role, Russia, I fear, may appear before the world as
                    the champion of all dependent peoples. Molotov’s move may confirm in the minds of the people of Asia
                    their already strong suspicion that the Anglo-American powers are not their real
                    champions and will turn to Russia as their more outspoken friend and
                    spokesman.</p>
                <p>Although I am sure you have these thoughts in mind, I thought perhaps you would
                    like to have our own impression of the importance of Molotov’s statement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
